#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SE0083 expect=noViolation domain=TF
#note "PLAN-join-key-one-side-absent-drop QK18 (3) (owner 2026-10-11): DS without USUBJID does NOT reach the QK16 ERROR for FDA-SE0083 - the Check's leading `USUBJID in $ds_usubjid` reads distinct(USUBJID, domain=\"DS\"), which holds no subject when DS lacks the column, so the conjunct is false on every record and the grouped DS extreme (group=[USUBJID]) is never read. Pinned as the measured answer: silent, no ERROR. Why it is data-dependent here (owner QK19, 2026-10-11): FDA-SE0083 has a rule-level Grouping, whose path has no absent-column fold reading the bindings up front, so the lazy grouped binding is read only behind the and short-circuit (E2) - the same Check without the Grouping ERRORs on this shape (measured on FDA-SE2270). A gate declaring DS.USUBJID would turn it into a SKIP."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
dataset TF class=FINDINGS label="Tumor Findings"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col TFSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TFTESTCD type=Char label="Tumor Findings Test Short Name"
col TFDETECT type=Num  label="Time in Days to Detection of Tumor"
---
S1 | TF | 001 | 1 | TUMEXAM | 120
S1 | TF | 002 | 1 | TUMEXAM | 50
---

dataset DS class=EVENTS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col DSSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSTERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Disposition Event"
col DSDECOD type=Char label="Standardized Disposition Term"
col DSSTDY  type=Num  label="Study Day of Disposition"
---
S1 | DS | 1 | REMOVED FROM STUDY ALIVE | REMOVED FROM STUDY ALIVE | 30
S1 | DS | 2 | TERMINAL SACRIFICE       | TERMINAL SACRIFICE       | 90
S1 | DS | 1 | TERMINAL SACRIFICE       | TERMINAL SACRIFICE       | 60

